643:
In the operation of a mobile car wash/auto detail business, it is unlawful for a principal, employee or agent of the business to:
(a) Create a nuisance under chapter 50 of this Code or an offense under chapter 54;
(b) Engage in washing the exterior of a vehicle upon any public street or public right-of-way, public property unless working specifically for said government or upon any vacant unimproved lot;
(c) Engage in washing or cleaning a motor vehicle engine;
(d) Advertise that services are available at a specific location, or otherwise invite customers to come to a specific location to receive services provided by the business;
(e) Erect or place advertising of the business at any location the business may operate;
(f) Operate at a fixed location;
(g) Violate any provision of state law or of the Municipal Code pertaining to water conservation; or
(h) Violate any provision of chapter 82, article V of this Code pertaining to the city's storm-water system.
(Ord. No. 628, § 1, 12-15-2015)

